# Secrets.
#
# .secrets/test.env holds a live API key. It must never be committed, and it is
# listed first so it is the first thing anyone reads here. If a key is ever
# staged by accident, rotate it: rewriting history does not un-leak a value.
#
# The CLI keeps its own credentials outside the repository, in ~/.Sael, so a
# working copy never holds one at all.
.secrets/
.env

# Build and test output.
/bin/
/dist/
/gateway/web/node_modules/
/gateway/web/dist/
/gateway/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
/gateway/var/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.out
*.test
*.prof

# A Go workspace, deliberately not committed.
#
# The two modules are joined by the replace directive in cli/go.mod, which works
# in a plain checkout. A committed go.work would be more convenient and is
# rejected for a specific reason: workspace mode is incompatible with
# GOFLAGS=-mod=mod, a setting from before Go 1.16 that is still common, and the
# failure it produces ("-mod may only be set to readonly or vendor when in
# workspace mode") does not hint at the cause. Anyone who prefers a workspace for
# editor support can create one locally; it will not be committed by accident.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
